    <briefdescription>
<para>MI-level patchpoint operands. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>MI patchpoint operations take the form: [&lt;def&gt;], &lt;id&gt;, &lt;numBytes&gt;, &lt;target&gt;, &lt;numArgs&gt;, &lt;cc&gt;, ...</para>
<para>IR patchpoint intrinsics do not have the &lt;cc&gt; operand because calling convention is part of the subclass data.</para>
<para>SD patchpoint nodes do not have a def operand because it is part of the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_s_d_value" kindref="compound">SDValue</ref>.</para>
<para>Patchpoints following the anyregcc convention are handled specially. For these, the stack map also records the location of the return value and arguments. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
